-- scripts/dst/driver_plus_compose_dst.ail
--
-- `driver_plus_compose` v1 acceptance (ADR-001 D5, WI-D27), and **the goal
-- line's clause 1 as an executable assertion.**
--
-- The machinery's own suite is scripts/dst/profile_definition_dst.ail; this
-- script asserts only what is true of THIS profile, and it is the first profile
-- acceptance script in the project that RUNS THE SUBJECT rather than only
-- reading its record.
--
-- ============================================================================
-- THE TWO HALVES, AND THE SECOND IS WHY THIS FILE IS NOT LIKE THE OTHER TWO
-- ============================================================================
--
-- **Half 1 — the record.** The same load `driver_only_dst` and
-- `driver_plus_no_ops_dst` perform: `validate_definition_at_load` at the table's
-- bound revision, against the measured HEAD inventory and the derived
-- classifier-2 call set, plus the four ADR-001 row-3 clauses that quantify over
-- installed extensions, each asserted twice — as it stands, and against a
-- MUTATION of this very definition that the clause must reject.
--
-- **Half 2 — THE DEMONSTRATION.** A full graded session through the REAL traced
-- driver with compose installed through `register_with_config`, recorded,
-- validated, reconstituted and STRICTLY REPLAYED. Every criterion-2 entry in
-- this profile's record names `discovery` as its basis, and `discovery` is an
-- EXISTENTIAL producer: its evidence is a run. **A profile citing it and not
-- running one is a basis with nothing behind it**, which is precisely the
-- fail-open shape `basis` was added to close. So the run is here, in the
-- profile's own gate, and not in a neighbouring suite.
--
-- ============================================================================
-- WHAT MAKES THE NON-VACUITY EXECUTABLE RATHER THAN COUNTED
-- ============================================================================
--
-- S21 counts four acceptance rows leaning on an empty install list, and WI-D13's
-- lesson is that **a vacuity that arrives with a number is the hardest kind to
-- see**. `driver_plus_no_ops` answered that with 32 covered hooks and a computed
-- statement saying none of them mediate. This profile answers it with ONE hook
-- that does, and one is not a number that reassures anybody — so it is asserted
-- rather than reported:
--
--     the recorded program contains >= 1 ExtensionEffect interaction whose
--     origin is `compose`, and the strict replay reproduces it
--
-- That row goes RED if compose is dropped from the install list, RED if the
-- intercept path breaks, RED if the recording regresses, and RED if the replay
-- diverges. It is the assertion the whole profile record rests on, and the
-- mutants below are run against it rather than against the record.
--
-- ============================================================================
-- WHAT THIS SCRIPT DOES NOT CLAIM
-- ============================================================================
--
-- Rows 1, 2, 6, 8, 9, 10 and 11 of ADR-001's acceptance table are NOT re-earned
-- here; a row not run is a row not earned and per D10 nothing transfers from
-- either predecessor. Compose is NOT classifier-clean and this script never says
-- it is — `make ext_ambient_inventory` reports it AMBIENT at 8 sources, and the
-- profile's header enumerates all 8. Door 3 is untouched.

